y I, who was raised to the rank of a Prince of the Holy Roman Empire in 1218. Ruled by Ascanian princes from the High Middle Ages to the Early modern period, Anhalt was divided several times amongst various lines of the dynasty until the dissolution of the Empire in 1806, when Napoleon elevated the remaining states of Anhalt-Bernburg, Anhalt-Dessau and Anhalt-Köthen to duchies."},{"qid":"Q155578","from_t":1806,"to_t":1878,"method":"name-label+date","confidence":0.95,"label":"Anhalt","description":"region in Central Germany, former state of the German Reich","inception":1806,"dissolved":1918,"enwiki":"Anhalt","summary":"Saxony-Anhalt (  ... AHN-hahlt; German: Sachsen-Anhalt [ˌzaksn̩ ˈʔanhalt] ; Low German: Sassen-Anholt) is a landlocked state of Germany. It covers an area of 20,555 square kilometres (7,936 sq mi)\nand has a population of about 2.14 million inhabitants, making it the 8th-largest state in Germany by area and the 11th-largest by population. Saxony-Anhalt borders the states of Brandenburg, Saxony, Thuringia and Lower Saxony."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q16155815","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q16550783","value_label":"Duchy of Anhalt","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Duchy of Anhalt"},{"qid":"Q16155815","kind":"coat","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Arms of the house of Anhalt (15th century).svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P94","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q155578","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q487070","value_label":"Dessau","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Dessau"},{"qid":"Q155578","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q1418514","value_label":"Gau Serimunt","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P155","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Gau Serimunt"},{"qid":"Q155578","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flagge Herzogtum Anhalt.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"